// pfodWeb NOTE: excludes GPIO7/21 - internal power-gate lines
// (I2C_POWER/NEOPIXEL_POWER), not general-purpose. Confirmed via vendor
// pins_arduino.h (I2C_POWER=7, NEOPIXEL_POWER=21):
// https://github.com/espressif/arduino-esp32/blob/master/variants/adafruit_feather_esp32s2/pins_arduino.h
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO13 tagged "led_high" - confirmed active-high user
// LED (LED_BUILTIN=13; https://learn.adafruit.com/adafruit-esp32-s2-feather/pinouts
// - "labeled #13", digitalWrite HIGH turns it on). GPIO33 tagged
// "led_neopixel" - confirmed onboard NeoPixel (PIN_NEOPIXEL=33, same
// pins_arduino.h).
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO0 tagged "button" - confirmed onboard BOOT
// pushbutton, documented as usable in application code (not just
// bootloader entry):
// https://learn.adafruit.com/adafruit-esp32-s2-feather/read-a-push-button
// - "This example uses the board's built-in push-button ... located
// under the STEMMA port and labeled BOOT."
